„­bible_version£KJV¤book§chapter¨sections•…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÛWhen thou goest out to battle against thine enemies, and seest horses, and chariots, and a people more than thou, be not afraid of them: for the LORD thy God is with thee, which brought thee up out of the land of Egypt.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqAnd it shall be, when ye are come nigh unto the battle, that the priest shall approach and speak unto the people,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÁand shall say unto them, Hear, O Israel, ye approach this day unto battle against your enemies: let not your hearts faint, fear not, and do not tremble, neither be ye terrified because of them;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdfor the LORD your God is he that goeth with you, to fight for you against your enemies, to save you.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse	¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÛAnd the officers shall speak unto the people, saying, What man is there that hath built a new house, and hath not dedicated it? let him go and return to his house, lest he die in the battle, and another man dedicate it.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¯And what man is he that hath planted a vineyard, and hath not yet eaten of it? let him also go and return unto his house, lest he die in the battle, and another man eat of it.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¤And what man is there that hath betrothed a wife, and hath not taken her? let him go and return unto his house, lest he die in the battle, and another man take her.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÙAnd the officers shall speak further unto the people, and they shall say, What man is there that is fearful and fainthearted? let him go and return unto his house, lest his brethren's heart faint as well as his heart.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd it shall be, when the officers have made an end of speaking unto the people, that they shall make captains of the armies to lead the people.¦layout ªlast_verse	…¤book§chapter«first_verse
